          %p A few more definitions of the integers, as well as the statement of the dependent universal property of the integers, could be found in:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Egbert+Rijke"}> Egbert Rijke
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Homotopy+Type+Theory"} Introduction to Homotopy Type Theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.11082"} arXiv:2212.11082
          %p
            Some terms about specific kinds of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H-spaces"} H-spaces
            used to prove properties of the integers are defined in:
          %ul
            %li#BuchholtzEtAl2023
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrik+Buchholtz"}> Ulrik Buchholtz
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.+Daniel+Christensen"} J. Daniel Christensen
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jarl+G.+Taxer%C3%A5s+Flaten"} Jarl G. Taxerås Flaten
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Egbert+Rijke"} Egbert Rijke
              %em Central H-spaces and banded types
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2301.02636"}> arXiv:2301.02636
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            A formalization in terms of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"}> Mike Shulman
              ,
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://github.com/HoTT/HoTT/blob/master/Coq/HIT/Integers.v"} Integers.v
          %p
            (A different common formalization of integers in type theory is in a binary notation, as in the
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://coq.inria.fr/stdlib/Coq.ZArith.BinInt.html"} Coq standard library
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1(S^1)
          %p
            That one can construct the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers+type"} natural numbers type
            from the integers type can be found in:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christian+Sattler"}> Christian Sattler
              ,
              %em Natural numbers from integers
              (
              %a{:href => "https://www.cse.chalmers.se/~sattler/docs/naturals.pdf"}> pdf
              )
        .revisedby
